    "ref": "Charge 1(A)",
    "subject": "Abu Dhabi sponsorship agreements",
    "period": "2009/10 to 2017/18",
    "finding": "proven",
    "appeal": "none",
    "summary": "The Commission found the sponsorship agreements were shams: each sponsor paid only part of the recorded fee and the club's owner, ADUG, paid the rest. Accounts submitted to the League overstated income by more than £830 million and did not give a true and fair view.",
